{
    "background_story": "Evie was a tiny, iridescent fly who lived in a bustling garden filled with vibrant flowers. As a member of the Muscoidea family, she was known for her distinctive housefly-like appearance and impressive flying skills. Evie's life was a whirlwind of activity, flitting from bloom to bloom in search of sweet nectar and warm sunshine. But despite her carefree existence, she had a secret passion - music. At night, when the garden grew quiet, Evie would sneak into the nearby conservatory and listen to the sounds of the nocturnal insects. Entranced by the melodies, she began to hum along, creating her own tiny harmonies. Soon, a group of fireflies discovered her talent and invited her to join their bioluminescent orchestra. Evie's love of music brought her fame among the garden's insect community, and she became known as the 'Muscoidea songstress'.",
